WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.240
AJA HAMMERLY: In
today's "Cloud Minute,"

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:02.864
I'm going to show
you how to view audit

00:00:02.864 --> 00:00:04.390
logs on Google Cloud.

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:05.800
From the Cloud
console home page,

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:09.840
click Activity in the sidebar.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.727
Now you can see all the
activity on your project.

00:00:12.727 --> 00:00:14.310
You can use the
filters to restrict it

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.761
to certain types of activities,
such as just configuration

00:00:16.761 --> 00:00:17.260
changes.

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:26.300
By default, viewing data
access logs is turned off,

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.080
but you can turn it on here.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:30.730
To see the data
access logs, you'll

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:34.750
need the private logs
viewer IAM permission.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:37.640
You can also restrict your logs
to just a specific resource

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.420
type, like GCEVM instances.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.320
Or you can filter by email.

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.360
You can even see audit
logs across projects,

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.040
if you need to.

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.590
Audit logs can also be accessed
from Stackdriver logging

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:56.852
if you want to create alerts
based on certain activities.

00:00:56.852 --> 00:00:58.810
I hope this helps you
keep track of your system

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:01.170
more efficiently.

